{
  "$schema": "./schema.json",
  "day": 38,
  "level": 3,
  "title": { "en": "Breakfast and paying", "es": "Desayunar y pagar" },
  "objectives": [
    "Order a Madrid bar breakfast",
    "Ask to pay: ¿Me cobras? ¿Cuánto te debo?",
    "Say how you'll pay: con tarjeta or en efectivo"
  ],
  "teach": [
    {
      "kind": "note",
      "md": "**A Madrid bar breakfast** is quick and standing up:\n\n- **un café con leche** or **un cortado**\n- **una tostada con tomate**: toast with grated tomato, olive oil and salt\n- or **un pincho de tortilla**: a wedge of tortilla de patatas\n\nMany bars do a breakfast deal: coffee + toast for a few euros, often on a board by the door."
    },
    { "kind": "phrase", "es": "¿Me pones un café con leche y una tostada con tomate?", "en": "Can I have a white coffee and toast with tomato?", "note": "Usually you get two halves of a large roll. Media tostada = just one half." },
    { "kind": "phrase", "es": "Un pincho de tortilla, por favor.", "en": "A slice of tortilla, please.", "note": "pincho = a single portion, here one slice. Ask for it caliente if you want it warmed up." },
    {
      "kind": "note",
      "md": "**Asking to pay.** In a bar you pay at the end, at the counter or at your table:\n\n- **¿Me cobras?** Can I pay? (literally *Will you charge me?*)\n- **¿Cuánto te debo?** How much do I owe you?\n\nBoth use *tú*, which is normal with bar staff. *¿Cuánto es?* (day 9) works too."
    },
    { "kind": "phrase", "es": "¿Me cobras, por favor?", "en": "Can I pay, please?", "note": "The most Spanish way to ask. Say it as the barman passes." },
    { "kind": "phrase", "es": "¿Con tarjeta o en efectivo?", "en": "By card or in cash?", "note": "What they'll ask you. Answer: Con tarjeta. Cards and phone payments work almost everywhere in Madrid, even for one coffee." },
    {
      "kind": "note",
      "md": "**Tipping** is small in Spain. In a bar, leaving the coins from your change is plenty. Nobody expects a percentage.\n\nWhen you hand over the money or the card: **Aquí tienes** (here you are)."
    }
  ],
